message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Energy-Flow Cosmology: Regime-Transition Fit to DESI DR2 BAO With Cross-Validation"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Magnusson"
    given-names: "Morten"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4860-5095"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Norway"
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-02-01"
doi: "10.6084/m9.figshare.31230703"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/supertedai/EFC"
keywords:
  - "Energy-Flow Cosmology"
  - "DESI DR2"
  - "BAO"
  - "regime transition"
  - "dark energy"
  - "Hubble tension"
  - "cross-validation"
abstract: >
  EFC regime-transition model fit to DESI DR2 BAO data.
  The model modifies the Friedmann equation as
  E²(z) → E²(z) × [1 + α_L2 × f(z) × Θ(z)],
  introducing a smooth transition at z ≈ 1.0.
  Best-fit: z_L1L2 = 1.01 ± 0.08, α_L2 = 0.045 ± 0.012.
  Δχ² = -8.4 compared to ΛCDM, with consistent
  cross-validation against Pantheon+ and cosmic chronometers.
